Notebook[{
Cell["PadicLazy", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"0a258c00-6f0c-4b67-96ab-1fcfee4482e5"],

Cell["\<\
PadicLazy[expr,p] stores exact rational leaves and inactive Plus, Times, \
Minus, integer Power, and square-root Power[expr,1/2] nodes in prime base p. \
Sqrt chooses the unit root 1 modulo 4 at p=2, or the smaller root modulo an \
odd prime. PadicN[s,p,n] requests n relative digits and obtains extra source \
precision when needed. Normal certifies a rational value; a genuinely \
irrational root expression returns Missing[\"NotRational\"]. Root recipes \
remain tied to their prime base. First[s] exposes the recipe for InputForm or \
TreeForm. Direct construction does not validate the recipe. Display previews \
digits without discarding sources.\
\>", "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"1927785f-2e57-4b98-bac5-dc89c020a1f1"],

Cell["\<\
PadicN[r,p] creates a source leaf. Arithmetic preserves the source values in \
inactive binary operations, so FullForm and InputForm expose the actual \
recipe without private helper symbols. The second field is the prime base.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ed2c0ed5-0134-44d2-8ccc-76238a00ccbe"],

Cell["\<\
Use First[s] to inspect the recipe and TreeForm[First[s]] to visualize it. \
These do not request a finite snapshot. Activating a rational recipe performs \
ordinary rational arithmetic; activating a root recipe applies real/complex \
branch conventions and does not preserve its p-adic meaning.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"74e76222-e7df-429c-8145-d2391ce55791"],

Cell["\<\
A lazy value has no fixed precision. Display requests a preview; \
PadicN[s,p,n] requests a finite snapshot; Normal certifies a rational result \
when one exists; genuinely irrational root expressions give a NotRational \
missing value. Bounds can be conservative and evaluating a large recipe can \
be expensive.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9c8d2329-795e-4e70-9738-1407bc0f5a61"],

Cell["\<\
Rational leaves, inactive arithmetic and square-root nodes created by the \
constructors and operators are supported. This is a representation head, not \
a general held-expression evaluator. Prefer the constructor; direct head \
construction is not validated.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a275f39e-50f1-42c3-90b1-bb883afceae0"],

Cell["\<\
Root recipes choose branches by congruence and obtain extra source digits for \
binary square roots. Composed root recipes use annihilating polynomials to \
certify valuation and rationality; many nested roots may be expensive. Negate \
the result to select the other root. Algebraic recipes cannot be implicitly \
converted between primes.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5b6e8a95-6b0a-4683-a08a-68b0ebb99d2e"],

Cell[BoxData[
